{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>She deals harshly with her young</b> — the meaning is that she is cruel toward her young, as though they were not hers, like 'you hardened yourself against them out of fear' [cf. Job 6:14]. And there is no third [instance] in Scripture." "<b>Her labor is without fear</b> — she has no fear for the eggs, lest her young trample them [with] foot."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:14.415435691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}